Brighter Pocket Companion installs with Local signing by default; Developer service is the fallback.

With pocket/patches/0009, tools/install.sh builds and copies a Local signing page container
for Brighter Shores (TOLKARA_MODE=local-signing): nothing to enrol, no tunnel, no
VPN-configuration prompt. The setup app now keeps an execution mode (SetupState.mode, Local
signing unless the user chose otherwise) and writes it to local.env. The Install step
offers the choice, with Developer service as the fallback for when the game does not start
with Local signing; only Developer service enrols (tools/enroll.sh) and only its Play steps
name the VPN configuration. A build records the mode it was made for, so changing it builds
again; when Tolkara was already on the device, a launch with --execution-mode and
--save-execution-mode makes the device's saved choice follow, since the build's
preselection applies only to a new install. Local signing's container is made for one
executable: the library's Update already builds again when the executable changed, and a
copy (Copy Game, Copy Again) now does too before it copies. The app on the device is called
Brighter Pocket (pocket/patches/0022), so the Play step, the Open buttons and the Files path
say so, and an install named Brighter Pocket is recognised as Tolkara. Not an upstream
candidate as it stands (it builds on 0021); the mode choice and the rebuild before a copy
are general.

